   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( g \\) be the function defined by \\( g(x) = \\int_{0}^{x} \\left(\\sin t + \\cos t\\right) \\, dt \\) for \\( 0 < x < 2 \\pi \\). Find the value of \\( x \\) at which \\( g \\) has a relative maximum."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Divide",
         [
            "Multiply",
            3,
            "Pi"
         ],
         4
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, \\( g'(x) = \\sin x + \\cos x \\) for \\( 0 < x < 2 \\pi \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Sin",
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Cos",
               "x"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Set \\( g'(x) = 0 \\): \\( \\sin x + \\cos x = 0 \\). The solutions in \\( 0 < x < 2 \\pi \\) are \\( x = \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\) and \\( x = \\frac{7 \\pi}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               3,
               "Pi"
            ],
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Only \\( x = \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\) and \\( x = \\frac{7 \\pi}{4} \\) lie in \\( 0 < x < 2 \\pi \\); \\( x = - \\frac{5 \\pi}{4} \\) is outside the interval on which \\( g \\) is defined, so it is not a critical point of \\( g \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               3,
               "Pi"
            ],
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "\\( g' \\) changes from positive to negative at \\( x = \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\) and from negative to positive at \\( x = \\frac{7 \\pi}{4} \\), so \\( g \\) has its relative maximum at \\( x = \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               3,
               "Pi"
            ],
            4
         ]
      }
